<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	25.47	    +109	    25.00     25.75</p>
<p>91-Day	29.37	    +130	    29.00     29.44</p>
<p>182-Day     31.74	    +133	    31.46     31.95</p>
<p>364-Day     32.43				32.00     32.90</p>
<p>Last week the 336-day paper was assigned at 30.94 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   2.28 bln pesos     2.53</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   3.99 bln pesos     4.43</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   3.84 bln pesos     4.27</p>
<p>364-Day     600 million pesos   1.40 bln pesos     2.33</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.49 on demand of 11.51 billion pesos, compared with 3.54 the week before, on demand of 11.70 billion pesos.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   28 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    7 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  21 basis points</p>
<p>    364-Day			  47 basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559. e-mail at robert.kozak@reuters.com</p>
